                </Paragraph>
              </ns5:DestinationCountryInformation>
              <ns5:DestinationCountryInformation SubTitle="PASSPORT EXEMPTIONS">
                <Paragraph Name="1">
                  <Text>PASSENGERS WITH A SEAMAN BOOK ISSUED BY AND ISSUED TO NATIONALS OF FRANCE, TRAVELING ON DUTY.</Text>
                </Paragraph>
              </ns5:DestinationCountryInformation>
              <ns5:DestinationCountryInformation SubTitle="VISA">
                <Paragraph Name="1">
                  <Text>VISA REQUIRED, EXCEPT FOR VISA IS NOT REQUIRED ONLY IF THE NATIONALITY OF MERCHANT SEAMEN IS MENTIONED UNDER VISA EXEMPTIONS APPLICABLE TO NORMAL PASSPORT HOLDERS. MERCHANT SEAMEN MUST BE ARRIVING TO BELGIUM IN ORDER TO BOARD A SHIP, WHICH MUST BE LOCATED IN A BELGIAN HARBOR; OR PROCEED TO AN AIRPORT IN THE SCHENGEN AREA  T*RGL/SCHN FOR RETURN, AFTER BEING DISCHARGED FROM A SHIP.</Text>
                </Paragraph>
                <Paragraph Name="2">
                  <Text>WARNING: MERCHANT SEAMEN MUST TRAVEL ON DUTY AND HAVE A LETTER OF EMPLOYMENT OR A LETTER OF GUARANTEE ISSUED BY THE SHIPPING COMPANY.</Text>
